Development-only dependencies (not distributed with the deployed Worker) include
wrangler, vitest, typescript, and @cloudflare/workers-types, each under its own
license as declared in its package metadata.

The MCP core (the two-tool shape, response field filtering, API-key redaction,
upstream error classification, and the distributed rate limiter) derives from a
single-owner Parcel connection originally built for ChatGPT's hosted apps. This
project reworks that logic into a portable Cloudflare Worker with pluggable
authentication. No credentials, owner identity, or deployment configuration from
that original are included.
